# Model, key check and 8s deadline live in services/pulse_llm.jac (LLM_MODEL in .env).
def llm_parse_filters(text: str, prior: FilterSpec, allowed_categories: list[str]) -> FilterSpec by pulse_llm.brief_llm(temperature=0.1, max_output_retries=1);
sem llm_parse_filters = "Turn an Ann Arbor resident's natural-language request into graph filters. Follow-ups like 'anything with food?' or 'add music' must ADD to the prior filters, not reset them. Set categories whenever the request names a topic that fits one, and leave them empty only when none fits: social = meeting people, making friends, hanging out, parties, game nights, social stuff; music = concerts, jazz, bands, shows; food = eating, brunch, dinner, tastings, markets; outdoor = hikes, parks, the river; sports = games, pickup, running; arts = galleries, theater, art walks; academic = lectures, talks, maker nights; networking = careers, jobs, internships, mixers; civic = council, votes, ordinances, hearings; community = neighborhood and city happenings. kinds may only contain event (things to attend), alert (road closures, lane closures, detours, bus reroutes), civic (council votes, ordinances, hearings) and organizer (clubs, groups); for things to do (stuff, events, activities, plans, where to go) set kinds to event; leave kinds empty only when the request is about everything. For closures, detours or buses set kinds to alert and leave categories empty (alerts are not tagged civic). For council, votes or hearings set kinds to civic. price is any, free or under10 (cheap or under 10 dollars means under10). time is today (today, tonight), weekend (Friday, Saturday, Sunday, the weekend) or week. distance is miles from campus (0 means any; near campus means 1). reply is one short friendly sentence that describes exactly the filters you set, and nothing you did not set.";
sem llm_parse_filters.text = "The user's request.";
sem llm_parse_filters.prior = "The filters currently active in the app.";
sem llm_parse_filters.allowed_categories = "The only category names that may appear in categories.";
